        <mxCell id="fnote" parent="1" style="text;html=1;fontSize=11;fontColor=#4A5563;align=left;fontStyle=2;" value="FK* columns referencing public.users(id) — owner_id (partners, leads), assigned_by (partner_roles), assigned_to (svc_cases, hd_tickets), logged_by (lead_activities, svc_case_activities), sender_id (hd_ticket_messages), merged_by (partner_merge_log) — are real foreign keys but point to Laravel&#39;s own users table, which lives outside the CRM schema and is not drawn here (no edge). svc_cases.subject_type / subject_id are deliberately plain informational columns, not a foreign key — CRM never reaches into a vertical module&#39;s schema (§5); resolving the pointer (e.g. subject_type = &#39;legal.case_hdrs&#39;) happens in that module&#39;s own controller layer, so no edge is drawn for it either." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1458" width="1400" height="70" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
